;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "A new reference grammar of modern Spanish (2019)"
 :source "Espanol/A new reference grammar of modern Spanish (2019).pdf"
 :page 64
 :exercises "Aligned example pairs, the FW11 fix landed.  Usage examples set
Spanish on the left and the English rendering on the right, and the
page mixes both servings: the (b) blocks arrive row-interleaved with
tab-joined continuation rows, the (c) and (d) blocks lane by lane.
The multicolumn pass reads both as two-cell rows - row-served rows
directly, lane-served ones through the ragged 1:1 pair gate - and
renders each pair as an org table row, wrapped cells and citations
joined into their cell.  The dropped line is the folio-merged
running head."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0))
